  "term": "BIS",
  "definition": "BIS is an EEG-derived measure of brain activity used here as an indirect marker of trance-like states during a mind-body intervention. In this context, lower BIS values were taken to suggest greater involvement in trance, although the measure showed substantial variation within and between people.",
